; The ONE variable: `line_length_guidelines` on a CodeEdit.
;
; `_draw_guidelines` (`code_edit.cpp:288-313`) rules the whole control height
; at each authored column, under the text (`text_edit.cpp:1319-1322`). The
; column's own x is `xmargin_beg + get_string_size("0".repeat(column)).x`, and
; both band tests are STRICT, so a column at 0 lands exactly on `xmargin_beg`
; and draws nothing while one past `xmargin_end` is dropped.
;
; `Ruled` authors four columns: 0 (drawn nowhere, the strict lower bound), 8
; and 16 (both inside the band), and 400 (past `xmargin_end`, the strict upper
; one). That array also pins the colour rule — `i == 0` keeps the full
; `line_length_guideline_color` and every later one halves its alpha
; (`:305`) — which the two visible rules show as two DIFFERENT intensities,
; since the full-colour one is the dropped column's successor, not the first
; drawn.
;
; `Plain` is the same CodeEdit with no array at all, so a regression that
; ruled unconditionally shows there and nowhere else. The alpha is 0.1 before
; the halving, so the fixture's own dark backdrop is what makes either rule
; readable at all.

